n the Bay Area Museum of Art Facts, Figures & Rankings Colleges that Changes Lives Notable Alumni Student Outcomes Athletics Athletics Athletics Athletic Calendar Buy Tickets Gael Force Kids Camps Men's Division 1 Athletics Baseball Swimming Waterpolo Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Tennis Track & Field Women's Division 1 Athletics Basketball Swimming Waterpolo Beach Volleyball Cross Country Rowing Soccer Softball Tennis Track & Field Volleyball Club Sports Join a Club Sport Club Sport Manual Give to Club Sports Men's Club Sports Men's Club Baseball Men's Lacrosse Men's Rugby Men's Club Soccer Men's Water Polo Co-Ed Club Tennis Co-ed Club Golf Women's Club Sports Women's Lacrosse Women's Club Soccer Women's Rugby STUNT Women's Water Polo Women's Volleyball Co-ed Club Tennis Co-ed Club Golf Faculty Directory Newscenter Events Alumni Parents & Families Apply Give Request Info Visit MySMC Search Menu Site Search Search Faculty Directory NewsCenter Events Alumni Parents & Families MySMC Student Life Vice President for Student Life Image Student Life Student Leadership Awards Student Enhancement Fee 2023-2024 Enhancement Fee 2024-2025 Enhancement Fee 2025-2026 Enhancement Fee Housing & Dining Residential Experience Meal Plan Information Dining Hours & Locations Housing and Meal Costs Activities & Clubs Planning Campus Events Campus Recreation Associated Students Campus Activities Board Student Government Residence Hall Association Student Clubs Intramural Leagues Wellness & Belonging Counseling and Psychological Services Student Health Center 24/7 TimelyCare The CARE Center Safety Resources Alcohol and Other Drugs (AOD) Nutritional Support Social Support Bias Incident Response Wellness Wednesday Programs Report & Support More Community Life & Essential Needs Life in the Bay Area Public Transportation New Student Experience First Year | First Six First-Year Experience The Gael Way Menu Student Life Student Leadership Awards Student Enhancement Fee 2023-2024 Enhancement Fee 2024-2025 Enhancement Fee 2025-2026 Enhancement Fee Housing & Dining Residential Experience Meal Plan Information Dining Hours & Locations Housing and Meal Costs Activities & Clubs Planning Campus Events Campus Recreation Associated Students Campus Activities Board Student Government Residence Hall Association Student Clubs Intramural Leagues Wellness & Belonging Counseling and Psychological Services Student Health Center 24/7 TimelyCare The CARE Center Safety Resources Alcohol and Other Drugs (AOD) Nutritional Support Social Support Bias Incident Response Wellness Wednesday Programs Report & Support Community Life & Essential Needs Life in the Bay Area Public Transportation New Student Experience First Year | First Six First-Year Experience The Gael Way Breadcrumb Home Student Life Image Image Credit Sofia Mastroianni Welcome from the Offices of the Vice President for Student Life & the Dean of Students! The Vice President oversees the vibrant departments of the Student Life Division. Student Life intersects at multiple points of a student's journey at Saint Mary's. With areas that promote students' living experiences, wellness, and engagement, Student Life accompanies students on their academic and co-curricular journey at Saint Mary's. The Division of Student Life creates a sense of belonging, offers participatory opportunities, and encourages students to contribute back their talents. Departments within Student Life include Campus Assault, Response, and Education (CARE), Campus Housing, Campus Recreation & Club Sports, the Career Center, Center for Women & Gender Equity, Counseling and Psychological Services, the Dean of Students & Community Life Office, Intercultural Center, New Student & Family Programs, Campus Safety & Transportation, Residential Experience, Student Disabilities Services, Veterans Services, Student Activities and Engagement, and the Student Health Center. The Office of the Dean of Students is a department within the division of Student Life and serves as a key link between students and other areas of campus life. The purpose is to support the out-of-classroom experiences of students in an effort to develop independent, civic-minded, and responsible adults. The Dean of Students staff coordinates the College’s response to crisis situations that involve students and frequently serves as liaisons between students, faculty, and other administrators or offices in many different situations. Image Image Credit Sofia Mastroianni Annual Report The 2022-2023 academic year was a successful year for the Division of Student Life! Learn more about the Division and its achievements in our Division of Student Life 2022-2023 Year in Review-compressed.pdf The Fall 2023 summary report can be found below. Student Enhancement Fee What does an undergraduate student's enhancement fee provide? The Student Enhancement fee is applicable to undergraduates and the funds go directly to Student Life to help subsidize important student activities such as events and concerts, cultural programs, wellness programs, and other student initiatives. Get Connected Get Connected by exploring the campus-wide event calendar, stopping by the Student Activities & Engagement Office (Ferroggiaro Hall) or visiting with the Residential Experience staff. Tips for Student Success Your success is our priority. Use this Quick Information Guide and navigate the information detailed throughout the SMC Student Life website for helpful information regarding academic resources, student engagement opportunities, and college-provided support services. Our Community Standards We uphold our Lasallian Core Values and align them with our community standards. If you have a concern for a student or wish to report a violation of The Student Handbook , use the links below. To notify college administration regarding a student of concern or to file a bias-related incident, complete and submit this reporting form . To report an alleged violation of The Student Handbook , complete and submit this incident referral form . Not sure where to report? Check out our report and support page . Image Image Credit Sofia Mastroianni Student Life Leadership Meet the 2026-2027 Student Life Leadership Team! Jim Sciuto , Ed.D. Vice President for Student Life Class of 2000, Class of 2022 (Ed.D.) Jessica Frazier Associate Vice President & Dean of Students Samantha Alberto Associate Dean for the Campus Experience Class of 2012 Dana Collins, Ph.D. Director of Counseling & Psychological Services Mitchell R. Foster Director of the Intercultural Center Megan Gallagher Director of Campus Assault, Referral & Education (CARE) & Wellness Initiatives Rebecca Harper Executive Director of Campus Recreation and Club Sports Nathan Johnson , Ed.D. Executive Director for Campus Safety and Transportation Travis Mason Associate Dean of Students/Director of Community Life Brian Middleton Director of Housing Operations & Auxiliary Services Erin Perkins , NP, Medical Director Student Health Center Onar Primitivo , Ed.D. Director of Student Activities & Engagement Sharon Sobotta Director of Center for Women & Gender Equity Vacant- new staff begins in October! Assistant Vice President for Student Support Services Mary Beth Stadt Executive Director of Career Center SMC Student Life 2025 Wowies 2025 Wowies 2025 Wowies Footer - Academics Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Footer - Admissions Admissions Apply Request Information Contact Admissions Resources Resources Library Bookstore Museum of Art Careers at SMC For the Media Footer - Financial Aid Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Scholarships University Credit Union Campus Info Our Campus Campus Map Parking & Transportation Accessibility at SMC Land Acknowledgment Emergency Information Immigration Enforcement Image 1928 St. Marys Rd Moraga, CA 94575 (925) 631-4000 © 2026 Saint Mary’s College of California Legal Nondiscrimination Policy Privacy Policy Title IX Login"
