Museum of Art Facts, Figures & Rankings Colleges that Changes Lives Notable Alumni Student Outcomes Athletics Athletics Athletics Athletic Calendar Buy Tickets Gael Force Kids Camps Men's Division 1 Athletics Baseball Swimming Waterpolo Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Tennis Track & Field Women's Division 1 Athletics Basketball Swimming Waterpolo Beach Volleyball Cross Country Rowing Soccer Softball Tennis Track & Field Volleyball Club Sports Join a Club Sport Club Sport Manual Give to Club Sports Men's Club Sports Men's Club Baseball Men's Lacrosse Men's Rugby Men's Club Soccer Men's Water Polo Co-Ed Club Tennis Co-ed Club Golf Women's Club Sports Women's Lacrosse Women's Club Soccer Women's Rugby STUNT Women's Water Polo Women's Volleyball Co-ed Club Tennis Co-ed Club Golf Faculty Directory Newscenter Events Alumni Parents & Families Apply Give Request Info Visit MySMC Search Menu Site Search Search Faculty Directory NewsCenter Events Alumni Parents & Families MySMC Academic Affairs Image About Meet the Provost Leadership & Staff Deans, Chairs, & Program Directors Annual Themes Events & Communications Resources Academic Policies & Procedures Accreditation & Affiliations Academic Calendars Institutional & Educational Effectiveness Program Review & Assessment Guidelines Academic Programs Faculty Resources Student Resources Advising & Academic Planning Academic Success Course Catalogs High Potential Program Honors Program Menu About Meet the Provost Leadership & Staff Deans, Chairs, & Program Directors Annual Themes Events & Communications Resources Academic Policies & Procedures Accreditation & Affiliations Academic Calendars Institutional & Educational Effectiveness Program Review & Assessment Guidelines Academic Programs Faculty Resources Student Resources Advising & Academic Planning Academic Success Course Catalogs High Potential Program Honors Program On this page, you will find links to important information for faculty, staff, and our various partners, as well as useful information for those looking to learn more about academics at Saint Mary's and the people who create an enriching learning environment at the College. Image About Our Office Image Academic Policies & Procedures Image Academic Programs Image Events Image Faculty Resources Image Student Resources About Our Office The Office of Academic Affairs and its leadership team serve the faculty and staff of Saint Mary's College in support of student achievement and academic success. Learn more about the different roles and the members of our team that oversee the academic operations across the college through the links below. Image Meet the Provost → Image Deans, Chairs, & Program Directors → Image Leadership & Staff → Image Annual Themes → Image Academic Affairs Resources → Image Academic Affairs News & Notes → Back to top → Carol Ann Gittens, PhD, MBA Image Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs & Provost The Provost oversees school deans and other academic and program leads at the college, who develop and maintain a diverse curriculum, which includes the humanities, arts, sciences, social sciences, education, business administration, and nursing, serving traditional students and adult learners in both undergraduate and graduate programs. Learn more About the Provost History From 1997-2017, Dr. Gittens served in a variety of senior leadership positions at Santa Clara University, including: Associate Dean, College of Arts & Sciences (2016-2017); Interim Chair, Sociology Department (2016-2017); Interim Dean, School of Education and Counseling Psychology (2015-2016); and Associate Dean, College of Arts & Sciences (2012-2015). At Saint Mary's, Dr. Gittens served as the Dean of SMC’s Kalmanovitz School of Education (KSOE) since 2019. There, she distinguished herself as a teacher, scholar, and leader with an impressive record of accomplishment. On December 4, 2024, SMC President Roger Thompson announced the appointment of Carol Ann Gittens , PhD, MBA as Acting Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost. Dr. Gittens began her tenure on January 1, 2025. On July 16, 2025, she was permanently appointed to the role. Scholarship Dr. Gittens's scholarship includes the publication of dozens of journal articles, research papers, and presentations. Topics include Critical Thinking and Information Literacy; Assessment of Student Learning; Higher Education Administration; and Teacher Education / Educational Psychology. Service Dr. Gittens actively serves in professional and community capacities as an Accreditation reviewer for the WASC Senior College and University Commission; member of the Board of Institutional Reviewers, California Commission on Teacher Credentialing; and as a former Trustee for the Morgan Hill Unified School Board of Education. She frequently serves as a manuscript reviewer and as both a strategic consultant and external program evaluator. Achievements Her achievements in higher education and at Saint Mary’s are numerous and align well with the responsibilities required of our Provost. In her role as Dean of KSOE, she has capably overseen financial planning and budgeting, personnel management, and a broad suite of academic programs. In addition, she: Led the School’s strategic planning process and helped ensure its alignment with SMC’s Transformation 2028 strategic plan; Helped establish an Endowed Professorship in Early Literacy Intervention and Reading Recovery while conducting a variety of fundraising and public outreach activities; Generated private foundation grants, oversaw the School’s scholarship award process, and revitalized a Lasallian Educator Fellowship program; Championed, co-hosted, and funded several Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging (DEIB) initiatives; Provided organizational leadership for two academic centers. Dr. Gittens's visionary leadership at KSOE solidified and advanced the School’s academic and institutional excellence through constructive and effective use of resources and a persistent pursuit of external funding opportunities. Her depth of experience will be key in supporting Saint Mary’s faculty, our schools, and our deans, while also helping to shape and drive our academic program offerings. More about Dr. Gittens's accomplishments as a higher education leader, including links to many of her scholarly papers and published articles, can be found on her academic website . Academic Affairs Leadership Shawny Anderson, PhD Vice Provost, Academic Affairs Milena Angelova PhD, EdD Director, Institutional Research Vidya Chandrasekaran, PhD Associate Vice Provost, Educational Effectiveness Allison Doyle Director, Academic Affairs Administration Elizabeth Gallagher, DMA Director, Office of Research Jeffrey A. Sigman, PhD Associate Vice Provost, Advising & Academic Success Academic Affairs Staff Vera Hammond Sustainability Coordinator Shane McCarthy Faculty Compensation Analyst Connor McCaslin Academic Data & Communications Specialist Chaitra Rao Coordinator, Institutional & Educational Effectiveness Andrea Solis Sustainability Coordinator Jump to: About Our Office → Deans, Chairs, & Program Directors Fall 2026 List Spring 2026 List Fall 2025 List Spring 2025 List Fall 2024 List Spring 2024 List Fall 2023 List Spring 2023 List Fall 2022 List 2021-2022 List Jump to: About Our Office → Annual Themes Image 2026-2027: Inclusive Community We celebrate diversity and welcome all members of our community. 2025-2026: Respect for All Persons We honor and respect the dignity of all individuals. At the heart of our work is the mission of Saint Mary’s College: to provide a transformative education rooted in the Lasallian, Catholic, and liberal arts traditions. One of our guiding principles, Respect for All Persons , served as the College’s institutional theme this year—a call to action for how we teach, learn, lead, and live together. Activities August Announce theme by President email Flier/Logo made Faculty morning discussion on Respect Mentioned at Welcome Liturgy August (Fall Semester) FYAC/TAC mission module emphasized the LCP and “respect.” Presented to 30 of 38 sections. September Intercultural Center and Library: You, Me, and We: Leading with Respect for Ourselves and Others Intercultural Center: Time to Strengthen Our Community. Collective Hour: Our Stories Told by Us October October 1: ODEI and Library film, 12:30 - 2 “The Illusionist” October 13: The upcoming book talk by Akhil Amar on 10/13. His new book Born Equal , explores how the idea that all Americans are created equal brought forth the Constitutional amendments that abolished slavery, secured Black and female citizenship, and extended suffrage regardless of race or gender. November Office of Mission and Staff Council co-sponsoring a reading and discussion on some “respect” grounded in Lasallian readings.   Likely November 18, 2 - 3 p.m. ODEI and Library, November 19, 12:30 - 2, film “You Throw Like A Girl” Jump to: About Our Office → Academic Affairs Resources Transformation 2028 Accreditation Center for Equity & Excellence in Teaching Office of Research EdTech Center Academic Faculty Senate Institutional Review Board Open Faculty Positions Back to top → Academic Policies & Procedures Academic Calendars Accreditation & Affiliations Program Review & Assessment Guidelines Academic Programs SCHOOLS School of Arts & Sciences School of Economics & Business Administration Kalmanovitz School of Education INSTITUTIONAL & SIGNATURE PROGRAMS Center for International Programs Study Abroad • International Student Services • Exchange Programs Collegiate Seminar Seminar Courses • Reading Lists • Enrichment Series Core Curriculum Core Course Designations • Core Requirements • Core Programs Engaged Learning EL Courses • Service Opportunities • Graduation Requirement January Term JAN Courses • Jan Term Travel • Course Schedules/Calendar Library Hours • Services • Special Collections Museum of Art Exhibitions • Collection • Hours Nursing Department First-Y